url: "https://raspberry-kim.github.io/donghyun-lab21/"
abstract: >-
  Donghyuns is a browser-based, noncommercial toy that follows only the
  broad frame of Strikers 1945 II (Psikyo, arcade, 1997): a vertically
  scrolling shooter on a tall 240x320 field with a shot, a three-level
  charge shot released by letting go of a held key, and a bomb, each
  different for the three aircraft (XF5U Flying Pancake, Ki-84 Hayate,
  P-38 Lightning); five stages, each with a mid-boss and a boss; and three
  difficulty levels (beginner, intermediate, advanced). The number of lives
  (1-9), the number of bombs (0-5), the starting stage (1-5) and the paper
  colour (rough cream or sketchbook white) are chosen through a program
  written in the esoteric programming language Donghyun-lang. Input is
  keyboard, touch and gamepad, with fullscreen; the game is saved in three
  browser slots and can be exported to and imported from a .dhsave file
  that includes every enemy, bullet and the random-number state. The only
  image file is the hand-lettered title on the start screen: every
  aircraft, enemy, boss, terrain and the paper grain is drawn by code as
  wobbly graphite strokes when the page opens, in greyscale on paper. No graphics, sound, text, stage layout, bullet data
  or code of the original game is used or extracted; all numbers are the
  author's own. The MIT license applies to the Donghyuns code and
  documentation; the page fonts are under the SIL Open Font License. See
  LICENSE and CREDITS.md.
keywords:
  - shoot 'em up
  - vertical shooter
  - procedural drawing
  - esoteric programming language
  - JavaScript
